{"shortDescription":"The Japanese yen strengthened to around 158 per dollar on Friday, recovering from two-week lows and snapping a five-session losing streak after Finance Minister Satsuki Katayama said President Donald Trump had expressed concerns about the yen during a meeting with Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi earl…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The Japanese yen strengthened to around 158 per dollar on Friday, recovering from two-week lows and snapping a five-session losing streak after Finance Minister Satsuki Katayama said President Donald Trump had expressed concerns about the yen during a meeting with Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi earlier this week."]},{"type":"p","children":["Markets were already alert to the possibility of intervention as the currency approached the key 160 level, which could test Tokyo’s tolerance for further yen weakness."]},{"type":"p","children":["Katayama reiterated that she would continue coordinating with her US counterpart Scott Bessent after Japan and the US carried out their first coordinated yen-buying intervention since 1998 in late July."]},{"type":"p","children":["The yen has faced renewed pressure as expectations for additional Federal Reserve rate hikes threaten to keep the US-Japan interest-rate differential wide."]},{"type":"p","children":["Uncertainty over the pace at which the Bank of Japan can continue tightening policy has also weighed on the currency."]}]},"language":"en","tags":[{"title":"Forex","args":[{"id":"category","value":"forex"}]},{"title":"Trading Economics","args":[{"id":"provider","value":"trading-economics"}]}],"id":"te_news:586815:0","title":"Yen Rebounds on Katayama Remarks","published":1790320029,"urgency":2,"link":"https://tradingeconomics.com/japan/currency","permission":"preview","relatedSymbols":[{"symbol":"FX:USDJPY","currency-logoid":"country/JP","base-currency-logoid":"country/US","logo":{"style":"pair","logoid":"country/US","logoid2":"country/JP"}},{"sym